# HTTP Assessment repository

This repository is the driver for solving an HTTP four-layer puzzle. 
The rest of the contents in this 'Readme' are running notes as the puzzle is being solved.

## Running notes

### Repository Structure
challenges/ - empty to start
src/
   data/ - empty to start; to hold any data discovered
   utils/
      log_config.py - sets up logging with two destinations - info+ in console and debug+ in session log
      submit.py - initially unwritten
   main.py - orchestrates endpoint discovery/requesting by command-line args
   session.log - to hold all logs for observability/trace
tests/
   test_client.py - tests apiClient and related funcs
.env
.gitignore
README - you are here
requirements.txt

Main parses arguments (mainly 'call') and routes respectively
ApiClient handles all HTTP and is logged in console (INFO+) along with file (DEBUG+)

